<title>CANADA: Methanex sees balanced Q2 methanol market.</title>
<headline>Methanex sees balanced Q2 methanol market.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Methanex Corp said the methanol market remained balanced to tight early in the second quarter, with strong methanol demand absorbing new production from its Chile II facility.</p>
<p>The company, which reported first quarter earnings of $0.27 per share compared to $0.08 per share in the year-ago first quarter, said the next large increment in methanol supply was the Statoil project slated to start up in mid-May.</p>
<p>&quot;Balance of supply and demand will ultimately depend on industry on-stream time, the strength of the global economy and, to a lesser extent, stable MTBE demand,&quot; it said.</p>
</text>
